From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: load the wireless config written at first boot

On a fresh install /etc/config/wireless does not exist when netifd
starts. The ieee80211 hotplug handler writes it with "wifi config" once
the radios show up, but netifd never reads it: "network.wireless retry"
only retries devices netifd already knows, so no radio comes up until
the next "wifi" or reboot. ath12k radios load seconds after netifd, so
every first boot (and every RAM boot) hits this.

Reload netifd when "wifi config" changed the file.

--- a/files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect
+++ b/files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect
@@ -1,6 +1,12 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
 [ "${ACTION}" = "add" ] && [ -f /etc/board.json ] && {
+	old=$(md5sum /etc/config/wireless 2>/dev/null)
 	/sbin/wifi config
+	# netifd only reads /etc/config/wireless when it starts or reloads.
+	# On a fresh install the radios show up after netifd has started, so
+	# load the sections that wifi config just wrote.
+	[ "$(md5sum /etc/config/wireless 2>/dev/null)" = "$old" ] ||
+		ubus call network reload
 	ubus call network.wireless retry
 }
